---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { resolvePrefs, ensureAnonId } from '../lib/prefs';
import { isMailConfigured } from '../lib/mail';
import { getIdentity, getPendingClaim } from '../lib/repo/auth';
import { pruneClaims } from '../lib/repo/auth';

// Must be the minted-and-set id, not a throwaway: this value goes in a hidden
// field and is what the claim endpoint attaches to, so a second, different id
// here would silently orphan the notes and saves the reader is claiming.
const anonId = ensureAnonId(Astro.cookies);
const prefs = resolvePrefs(Astro.cookies as never, anonId);
const identity = await getIdentity(Astro.cookies);
void pruneClaims();
const pending = await getPendingClaim(anonId);

const claimToken = Astro.url.searchParams.get('claim');
const mailedHandle = Astro.url.searchParams.get('mailed') ?? '';
const mailConfigured = isMailConfigured();

/* The token in the URL is the one just requested, so it wins. Falling back to the
   pending claim means the link also survives a reload or a later visit, which
   matters because requesting a claim immediately creates a pending claim — the
   page must not lose the only copy of the link it is supposed to show. */
const activeToken = claimToken ?? pending?.token ?? null;
const claimPath = activeToken ? `/claim/${activeToken}` : null;
---

<Base
  title="Write here"
  description="Why this publication is different, how the writing lifecycle works, and how to claim a handle."
  prefs={prefs}
>
  <header class="shell border-b border-rule py-12">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="meta">For writers</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl">Write here</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
        The pitch is narrow on purpose. If you write long-form on a subject where depth, argument and
        someone being accountable for accuracy actually beat short-form social, this place is built
        for you and almost nothing else.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="shell py-12">
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-14">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl">What is different</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
          <p>
            <strong class="font-medium text-ink">A post is a living document.</strong> Publishing is
            not an event. Corrections are recorded, versioned, and readable side by side, and readers
            who saw the old version are told what moved. A correction is not an embarrassment to
            patch quietly — on this site it is the most interesting thing a long-lived post can
            contain.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="font-medium text-ink">You write for three readers at once.</strong> Blocks
            are tagged in layers, so one post serves someone skimming for the argument, someone
            reading it properly, and someone who wants the footnotes. Currently most technical
            writing picks a single altitude and alienates half its audience.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="font-medium text-ink">You get told where readers got lost.</strong> Not a
            scroll heatmap — which block people reached is a better question, cheaper to answer, and
            it points at a different fix. Aggregate only, never shown for a group smaller than twenty
            readers, and no per-reader view for you to browse.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="font-medium text-ink">You keep the argument.</strong> Corrections and
            extensions from readers attach to specific sentences and survive you rewriting the
            paragraph. Accept one and it is folded into your revision history as an attributed
            amendment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl">What you will not get</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 border-l border-rule pl-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
          <li>No follower counts, no likes, no open rate theatre.</li>
          <li>No ad network and therefore no ad-shaped writing.</li>
          <li>
            No algorithmic feed. Discovery here is curation: reading lists with a reason for the
            order.
          </li>
          <li>
            No paywall in front of the core post. What can be gated is the supplementary layer —
            raw notebooks, extended cuts, the actual dataset.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
          Monetisation exists but it is not the product. If the only way this works is a wall, it
          does not work — that is how Medium killed its own network effect.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl">The lifecycle</h2>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-4 border-l border-rule pl-4">
          <li>
            <strong class="font-medium">Seedling.</strong>
            <span class="text-ink-2">
              {' '}An early thought, published before it is finished, on purpose. The point is to get
              something out there before it is ready, so the writing starts.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="font-medium">Budding.</strong>
            <span class="text-ink-2"> An argument forming, with references attached to its claims.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="font-medium">Evergreen.</strong>
            <span class="text-ink-2">
              {' '}Actively maintained, with a named maintainer and a review cadence. A post nobody
              has touched in six months says so — that is a nudge, not a badge of shame.
            </span>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
          The incentive is to maintain and connect work, not to chase publication volume. That is the
          whole structural difference from the medium you are used to.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="handle" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-xl">Your handle</h2>
        {
          identity.handle ? (
            <div class="mt-4 border border-pine px-4 py-3">
              <p class="text-[0.9375rem]">
                You are writing as{' '}
                <strong class="font-medium">@{identity.handle}</strong>. Your anonymous notes from
                this browser were attached when you claimed it.
              </p>
            </div>
          ) : pending ? (
            <div class="mt-4 border border-ochre px-4 py-3">
              <p class="text-[0.9375rem]">
                A claim for <strong class="font-medium">@{pending.handle}</strong> was requested from
                this browser and has not been redeemed yet.
              </p>
              {mailConfigured ? (
                <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem]">
                  {mailedHandle ? (
                    <>
                      The link is on its way to your inbox for{' '}
                      <strong class="font-medium">@{mailedHandle}</strong>. It expires in twenty
                      minutes, and asking for a new one replaces it.
                    </>
                  ) : (
                    <>
                      The link is in the email sent to you. It expires, and asking for a new one
                      replaces it.
                    </>
                  )}
                </p>
              ) : (
                <>
                  <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem]">
                    <strong>No mailer is configured on this site, so the link is here instead of in an inbox.</strong>{' '}
                    Set <code class="border border-rule bg-sunken px-1">BREVO_API_KEY</code> and a{' '}
                    <code class="border border-rule bg-sunken px-1">MAIL_FROM</code> matching the
                    sender you verified, and it travels by email like a real signup.
                  </p>
                  {claimPath && (
                    <p class="mt-2">
                      <a
                        href={claimPath}
                        class="border border-ink bg-ink px-3 py-1.5 text-[0.9375rem] text-paper no-underline transition-colors hover:border-accent hover:bg-accent"
                      >
                        Claim @{pending.handle} now →
                      </a>
                    </p>
                  )}
                </>
              )}
            </div>
          ) : (
            <>
              <p class="mt-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
                You do not need an account to read, and you never needed one to leave a margin note.
                If you have already written notes from this browser and want them attributed to a
                name, claim a handle and they are all attached at once — nothing is orphaned and
                nothing is recreated.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
                There are no passwords. A handle is a name attached to your notes, not a credential,
                so it cannot be phished and cannot be used to take over an account.
              </p>

              <form method="post" action="/api/claim" class="mt-5 border border-rule p-4">
                <input type="hidden" name="anon" value={anonId} />
                <p class="meta mb-2">Claim a handle</p>
                <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
                  <label class="block">
                    <span class="meta">Handle</span>
                    <input
                      name="handle"
                      required
                      pattern="[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_\-]{2,23}"
                      placeholder="yourhandle"
                      class="mt-1 w-full border border-rule bg-paper px-3 py-2 text-[0.9375rem] focus:border-accent focus:outline-none"
                    />
                  </label>
                  <label class="block">
                    <span class="meta">Email</span>
                    <input
                      name="email"
                      type="email"
                      required
                      placeholder="you@example.com"
                      class="mt-1 w-full border border-rule bg-paper px-3 py-2 text-[0.9375rem] focus:border-accent focus:outline-none"
                    />
                  </label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-[0.75rem] leading-snug text-ink-3">
                  3 to 24 characters: letters, numbers, dash or underscore. The email is only used to
                  send the claim link; it is not published anywhere.
                </p>
                <button
                  type="submit"
                  class="mt-3 border border-ink bg-ink px-3 py-1.5 text-[0.9375rem] text-paper transition-colors hover:border-accent hover:bg-accent"
                >
                  Send me the claim link
                </button>
              </form>
            </>
          )
        }
      </section>

      {
        identity.userId ? (
          <section id="import">
            <h2 class="text-xl">Importing an archive</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
              Switching cost is the archive, so import is step one. Bring Markdown with front
              matter — what Substack, Hashnode, Dev.to, Obsidian and Ghost all reduce to — or a
              WordPress XML export. Original publication dates and the address each post used to
              live at are kept, because a post re-dated to today is not an import, it is a lie about
              when you believed something.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-5 border border-rule bg-surface p-4" data-import>
              <label class="meta block" for="import-files">
                Markdown (.md, .markdown, .mdx, .txt) or WordPress XML (.xml)
              </label>
              <input
                id="import-files"
                type="file"
                multiple
                accept=".md,.markdown,.mdx,.txt,.xml,text/markdown,text/plain,application/xml,text/xml"
                class="mt-2 block w-full text-[0.9375rem] file:mr-3 file:border file:border-rule file:bg-paper file:px-3 file:py-1.5"
              />

              <details class="mt-4">
                <summary class="meta cursor-pointer text-ink-3 hover:text-ink">
                  Or paste one post
                </summary>
                <label class="sr-only" for="import-paste">
                  Paste a post
                </label>
                <textarea
                  id="import-paste"
                  rows="8"
                  placeholder="Paste Markdown with front matter…"
                  class="mt-2 w-full resize-y border border-rule bg-paper px-3 py-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed focus:border-accent focus:outline-none"
                />
              </details>

              <label class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-2">
                <input type="checkbox" data-import-draft class="h-4 w-4 accent-[var(--accent)]" />
                Import as drafts — keep the original dates off the listing until I review them
              </label>

              <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
                <button
                  type="button"
                  data-import-go
                  class="border border-ink bg-ink px-3 py-1.5 text-[0.9375rem] text-paper transition-colors hover:border-accent hover:bg-accent disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50"
                >
                  Import
                </button>
                <p class="meta" data-import-status aria-live="polite" />
              </div>

              <div class="mt-4" data-import-results hidden />
            </div>

            <p class="mt-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
              Imported posts land as <strong>budding</strong>, not evergreen: the content is real but
              nobody here has checked it, and this publication does not mark something as maintained
              without a reason. Every import records where it came from in the revision log, so you can
              see what was inferred and change any of it in the editor.
            </p>
          </section>
        ) : (
          <section>
            <h2 class="text-xl">Importing an archive</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
              Switching cost is the archive, so import is step one and it has to be excellent.
              Markdown with front matter — what Substack, Medium, Dev.to, Hashnode and Ghost all
              reduce to — and WordPress XML are supported, with original publication dates and
              inbound links preserved.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
              Claim a handle above and the import opens up. Bring the archive; the argument for
              switching is that everything you published finally has somewhere to keep changing.
            </p>
          </section>
        )
      }

      <p class="border-t border-rule pt-6 text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-2">
        Still interested?{' '}
        <a href="/about" class="text-ink no-underline hover:text-accent">
          How it works →
        </a>{' '}
        or read{' '}
        <a href="/lists/start-here" class="text-ink no-underline hover:text-accent">
          the starting order →
        </a>
        . {mailConfigured ? '' : 'Writer accounts open by invitation while the seed canon is in place.'}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      /* Archive import.
         Files are read in the browser with File.text() and sent as JSON, so the
         server parses exactly the bytes that were on disk and nothing is written
         to a temp directory on the way. Every outcome is listed per file: an
         import that quietly skipped half an archive is worse than one that
         failed loudly, and "which of my 90 posts did you actually take?" is the
         first question anybody asks. */
      const root = document.querySelector('[data-import]');
      if (!root) return;
      const input = document.getElementById('import-files');
      const paste = document.getElementById('import-paste');
      const asDraft = root.querySelector('[data-import-draft]');
      const go = root.querySelector('[data-import-go]');
      const status = root.querySelector('[data-import-status]');
      const results = root.querySelector('[data-import-results]');
      if (!input || !go || !status || !results) return;

      const MAX_BYTES = 512 * 1024;

      function say(text) {
        status.textContent = text;
      }

      async function send(files) {
        if (files.length === 0) {
          say('Choose a file, or paste a post, first.');
          return;
        }
        go.disabled = true;
        results.hidden = true;
        results.innerHTML = '';
        say(`Reading ${files.length} file${files.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}…`);
        try {
          const res = await fetch('/api/import', {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({
              files,
              asDraft: asDraft ? asDraft.checked : false,
            }),
          });
          const body = await res.json();
          if (!res.ok) {
            say('');
            render([{ filename: 'request', imported: false, reason: body.error ?? 'Import failed.' }], 0, 0);
            return;
          }
          say(`Imported ${body.imported} of ${body.batch}.`);
          render(body.results, body.imported, body.failed);
          if (body.imported > 0) input.value = '';
        } catch {
          say('The import could not be sent. Check your connection and try again.');
        } finally {
          go.disabled = false;
        }
      }

      function render(rows, imported, failed) {
        results.hidden = false;
        results.innerHTML = '';
        const list = document.createElement('ul');
        list.className = 'mt-3 space-y-2 border-t border-rule pt-3 text-[0.875rem]';
        for (const r of rows) {
          const li = document.createElement('li');
          li.className = 'border-l-2 pl-3 ' + (r.imported ? 'border-pine' : 'border-danger');

          const head = document.createElement('p');
          head.className = 'font-medium';
          head.textContent = r.imported ? r.title || r.filename : `${r.filename} — not imported`;
          li.appendChild(head);

          const meta = document.createElement('p');
          meta.className = 'meta mt-0.5';
          if (r.imported) {
            const bits = [r.url];
            if (r.publishedAt) {
              bits.push(`original date kept: ${new Date(r.publishedAt).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}`);
            }
            if (r.draft) bits.push('saved as a draft');
            meta.textContent = bits.filter(Boolean).join(' · ');
          } else {
            meta.className = 'meta mt-0.5 text-danger';
            meta.textContent = r.reason ?? 'Unknown reason.';
          }
          li.appendChild(meta);

          for (const note of r.inferred ?? []) {
            const p = document.createElement('p');
            p.className = 'meta mt-0.5';
            p.textContent = note;
            li.appendChild(p);
          }
          list.appendChild(li);
        }
        results.appendChild(list);

        if (imported > 0) {
          const p = document.createElement('p');
          p.className = 'mt-3 text-[0.875rem]';
          const a = document.createElement('a');
          a.href = '/studio';
          a.className = 'text-ink underline hover:text-accent';
          a.textContent = 'Open the studio →';
          p.appendChild(a);
          results.appendChild(p);
        }
        if (failed > 0) {
          const p = document.createElement('p');
          p.className = 'meta mt-2';
          p.textContent = `${failed} file${failed === 1 ? '' : 's'} did not make it in. The reasons are above.`;
          results.appendChild(p);
        }
      }

      go.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const files = [];
        for (const f of Array.from(input.files ?? [])) {
          if (f.size > MAX_BYTES) {
            say(`${f.name} is larger than 512KB and was skipped.`);
            continue;
          }
          files.push({ filename: f.name, content: await f.text() });
        }
        const pasted = paste?.value.trim();
        if (pasted) files.push({ filename: 'pasted-post.md', content: pasted });
        await send(files);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
